</style>
<h2>Asobi Review 1.0 (build 2093) <span class="when">Nov 2, 2026</span></h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Every comment of a cut movie in one list:</b> the Notes tab's Whole movie lists every shot's comments; click a timecode to go there.</li>
<li>Comment subtitles are in the bar's Show menu too.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<div class="earlier">Earlier updates</div>
<h3>1.0 (build 2089) <span class="when">Nov 2, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Every shot of a long cut movie fits in the strip:</b> the last few shots no longer sit past the window's edge.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 2086) <span class="when">Nov 2, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Comments as subtitles:</b> press U, or use Subtitles in the bar, to show each note over the picture as it plays. Show ▸ Comment Subtitles ▸ Position puts them in any of nine places.</li>
<li>A cut movie's shots play from the movie's one review copy, fetched once.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 2079) <span class="when">Nov 2, 2026</span></h3>
<h2>Asobi Review 1.0 (build 2079)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Reviews of a cut movie, shot by shot:</b> you see the host's shots in the host's order, following them at their frame, from the movie or its review copy fetched once.</li>
<li><b>Every note is there when you join,</b> on every clip, not only the one the host is on.</li>
<li><b>Click from comment to comment</b> in the clip strip: a clip opens on its first note, the next click goes to the next.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 2060) <span class="when">Nov 2, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>See where the notes are on every clip:</b> the clip strip shows each clip's notes and marked frames, not only the one on screen.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 2057) <span class="when">Nov 2, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Small fixes</b> behind the scenes; reviewing works as before.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 2048) <span class="when">Nov 2, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>A cut movie plays straight through</b> in a review, without stopping at each shot.</li>
<li><b>Trimmed clips sound right</b> in reviews streamed from the host.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 2039) <span class="when">Nov 2, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Right frame in a live review.</b> On a trimmed clip or a shot of a cut movie, you now see the frame the host is on, and your notes and marks land where you made them.</li>
<li><b>Joining on the right frame.</b> Joining a review in progress takes you to the frame the room is on, with earlier notes and marks in place.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
